# .lycheeignore — URLs lychee should NOT check
#
# lychee reads exactly one .lycheeignore, so this file replaces the shared one
# from megalint-config rather than extending it. The first two entries are
# copied from the shared file (megalint-config v0.6.0); keep them in sync when
# re-pinning. One regular expression per line, matched against the URL.

# Shared: URLs assembled at runtime (`${VAR}`, `${{ ... }}`) are never
# substituted, so lychee requests an address that only exists once expanded.
^https?://.*(\$\{|\$%7B|\$$)

# Shared: in-toto predicate type URIs are namespace identifiers, not documents.
^https://cosign\.sigstore\.dev/attestation/

# polypkg's JSON Schema `$id` values are identifiers. polypkg.dev is not a
# published site; the schemas ship embedded in the binary.
^https://polypkg\.dev/schemas/

# Loopback addresses, with or without user:password, point at servers that
# exist only while a test runs: the e2e repository server in task and compose
# files, and the unreachable endpoints of the credential-redaction tests.
^https?://([^/@]+@)?(localhost|127\.0\.0\.1)([:/]|$)

# release.yml passes cosign an OIDC issuer (an identifier whose root path is
# 404) and a certificate-identity regex; lychee cuts the regex's `github\.com`
# at the backslash and requests `https://github/`.
^https://token\.actions\.githubusercontent\.com/?$
^https://github/?$
